Kangaroo Builder is a professional rigging framework for animation, VFX, and game production pipelines. While not strictly a computer vision project, it is closely related through its focus on geometry processing, spatial transformations, mesh analysis, deformation transfer, and technical pipeline engineering.

Developed and maintained independently by me, the system was designed to address complex production requirements in facial rigging, body rigging, procedural deformation workflows, and advanced geometry manipulation.

Kangaroo Builder has been commercially licensed and used in feature film productions, television projects, and game development environments.

The framework includes a broad range of production-oriented tools and techniques, including:

Facial and body rigging systems
Topology-independent mesh blending and deformation transfer (https://kangaroobuilder.com/landmarkWarp/)
Surface-aware deformers that slide across polygonal meshes using 3D pathfinding algorithms
Audio-driven lip-sync systems that convert speech into facial animation
Mesh-based weight transfer and procedural skinning tools (https://kangaroobuilder.com/tools/toolsPlaneCutter/)
Procedural rigging and geometry processing utilities for production pipelines
The entire architecture, implementation, maintenance, and long-term feature development of the framework have been handled independently by me since 2019.



